## #02 — One receipt check
`_require_stored_receipt` is the only identity check. `_read_stored_receipt` uses it on the file before status, replay, or recover asks the adapter to report that file. `_guard_reported_receipt` uses it again on the object about to be printed, when a receipt file exists. A missing file is left to the adapter. `unknown`, `accepted-not-launched`, and `uncertain` do not have to carry receipt fields.

A persisted receipt must be a strict JSON object with schema `worker-bridge/receipt@1`. `delivery_id`, `job_id`, `backend`, and `request_sha256` must be non-empty strings. `delivery_id` must equal the requested delivery, the provenance, and the stored request. `job_id` and `backend` must equal the provenance and the stored request. `request_sha256` must equal the provenance hash. Extra keys, including `artifacts`, `cleanup`, `recovered`, and `replayed`, stay allowed. The refusal is `stop:` on stderr, empty stdout, and exit 2. It does not rewrite the receipt and it does not launch. This is not a signature, an approval, or a second ledger. Status remains read-only.

